  "system": {
    "slug": "mordin-solus",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 7
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>Professor Mordin Solus is a salarian scientist, former STG operative, and one of the most brilliant minds in the galaxy. He is a man of many talents: geneticist, physician, soldier, and Gilbert-and-Sullivan enthusiast. He speaks very fast. He once helped modify the genophage. He has complicated feelings about this. In combat he is surprisingly lethal, combining tech powers with a rapid-fire SMG.</p><p><strong>Salarian Metabolism:</strong> Mordin gains a +2 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls and is never caught flat-footed in a surprise round.</p><p><strong>Incinerate (2 actions):</strong> One target within 60 feet takes 3d8+8 fire damage and is Clumsy 1 until the end of its next turn (DC 25 Reflex for half, no Clumsy on success).</p><p><strong>Neural Shock (2 actions, 1/encounter):</strong> One target within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 25 Fortitude save or be Stunned 1 (Stunned 2 on a critical failure).</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
